  "redaction_policy": [
    "Source Python and historical mock logs are byte-exact.",
    "JSON projections select necessary fields, replace private host roots with logical role tokens, and remove process-local object addresses.",
    "Every projection records the original source SHA and byte length; its own bytes are different and cannot be passed off as the original signed/approved/launchable input.",
    "Raw module dictionaries, maps, 18,622-file manifests, runtime/dependency binaries, wheels, model tensors and user inputs are excluded.",
    "A retained marshal/code hash was measured against the original source filename and interpreter; replacing a displayed path with a role does not recompute the hash or establish relocation equivalence."
  ],
